! QE's `test-suite/ph_interpol_metal/al.scf.in` with the symmetry switched off,
! the ground state of that directory's electron-phonon benchmark
! (`al.elph.in`, electron_phonon = 'simple'). fcc aluminium, norm-conserving LDA,
! Marzari-Vanderbilt at degauss = 0.05 Ry on the 8x8x8 unshifted grid. The grid
! is closed under the point group, so the whole-grid sum here equals ph.x's
! symmetrised wedge sum to the solves' residue. conv_thr is tighter than the
! reference's 1e-8, which a derived quantity needs (CLAUDE.md, "a test asserting
! a tolerance its own conv_thr does not deliver").
 &control
    calculation='scf'
 /
 &system
    ibrav=2, celldm(1)=7.5, nat=1, ntyp=1,
    ecutwfc=15.0, nosym=.true., noinv=.true.,
    occupations='smearing', smearing='marzari-vanderbilt', degauss=0.05
 /
 &electrons
    conv_thr = 1.0d-12
    mixing_beta = 0.7
 /
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 Al  26.98 Al.pz-vbc.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS crystal
 Al  0.3333333333333  0.6666666666667  0.0000000000
K_POINTS automatic
 8 8 8 0 0 0
